    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes. Let me verify my new count semantics against the intended behavior with a quick reasoning check, and confirm nothing else references the counting logic I refactored.\n\nThe implementation is complete and green. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: *\"When more than 80 owners have already been created today, include `bulkSignupWarning` true in the response; otherwise false.\"* Owners are created via the OfficeFloor `POST /api/owners` pipeline, and tests read the field back through `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 so the flag has to be computed at creation, persisted on the entity, and exposed on the response DTO.\n\nChanges, each kept to a single responsibility:\n\n1. **`FlagOwnerBulkSignup`** (new function class) \u2014 the one piece of new logic: counts owners already registered on the new owner's (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate` and sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. Wired into the pipeline as a new `flagBulkSignup` step after `requireDailyCapacity` (both need the resolved registration date), under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRegistrations`** (new shared helper) \u2014 extracted the \"count owners registered on a given day\" logic so it isn't duplicated. `RequireDailyRegistrationCapacity` now delegates to it too (removing its duplicated stream and unused import) \u2014 same behavior, one source of truth. This is the natural bucket both the hard daily cap and the soft bulk-signup warning share.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` Boolean column (getter/setter, `@Column`).\n\n4. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb is what the tests use with `ddl-auto=none`, plus h2/mysql/postgres for consistency).\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it; MapStruct maps it by name automatically (request-side `OwnerFieldsDto` is untouched).\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test (`coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold`) creates an owner and confirms `$.bulkSignupWarning == false` under the threshold.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: I interpreted \"created today\" as *owners sharing the new owner's registration date* \u2014 consistent with the existing `RequireDailyRegistrationCapacity` rule and the test harness's `createMany` (\"all dated today\") \u2014 rather than wall-clock `LocalDate.now()`. If the intended semantics are strictly wall-clock creation time, let me know and I'll adjust the count.",
